<h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-800 mt-8 mb-3 leading-snug font-display"><strong>16. Tungarli Lake</strong></h3>
<figure class="my-4"><img src="images/DiscoveringtheCharmofTungarliLak-1024x558.webp" alt="Tungarli Lake Lonavala" class="w-full rounded-lg shadow-md"></figure>
<p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed mb-5">A less commercialized and more pristine spot compared to Lonavala Lake, Tungarli Lake is a beautiful artificial reservoir that provides drinking water to the Lonavala town. It was built during the British era in the 1930s. The lake is surrounded by rugged terrain and dense forests, making it an excellent spot for camping, backpacking, and solitary nature walks away from the tourist crowds.</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-700 mb-5">
    <li><strong>Things to do:</strong> Lakeside camping, sunset viewing, photography, and short nature treks.</li>
    <li><strong>Best time to visit:</strong> Post-monsoon and winter months when the lake is full and the weather is crisp.</li>
    <li><strong>How to reach:</strong> It is about 3-4 kilometers from Lonavala station; you can trek or take a vehicle up the bumpy road.</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-800 mt-8 mb-3 leading-snug font-display"><strong>17. Pawna Lake</strong></h3>
<figure class="my-4"><img src="images/Pawna-Lake-Camping-Lonavala.webp" alt="Pawna Lake" class="w-full rounded-lg shadow-md"></figure>
<p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed mb-5">Located slightly off the main town of Lonavala, Pawna Lake has emerged as the premier spot for lakeside camping in Maharashtra. Formed by the Pawna Dam, this massive artificial lake is surrounded by high towering forts like Tikona, Lohagad, and Tung. Watching the sunset here by a crackling bonfire, with live acoustic music and a barbeque, is an essential <strong>weekend getaway from Mumbai</strong> experience. For more on this, read our <a href="/pawna-lake-camping-lonavala-complete-guide-with-stay-option.php" class="text-amber-600 hover:underline">complete guide to Pawna Lake camping</a>.</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-700 mb-5">
    <li><strong>Things to do:</strong> Overnight camping, stargazing, boating, kayaking, and bonfire barbeques.</li>
    <li><strong>Best time to visit:</strong> Winters (November to February) for the best camping experience.</li>
    <li><strong>How to reach:</strong> Best accessed by private vehicle, located around 20 kilometers from Lonavala.</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-800 mt-8 mb-3 leading-snug font-display"><strong>18. Ekvira Devi Temple</strong></h3>
<figure class="my-4"><img src="images/Lonavala-for-Culture-Seekers-Explore-Caves-Temples-Local-Markets.jpeg" alt="Ekvira Devi Temple" class="w-full rounded-lg shadow-md"></figure>
<p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed mb-5">Situated adjacent to the ancient Karla Caves, the Ekvira Devi Temple is a highly revered Hindu shrine, particularly significant to the Koli (fishermen) community of Maharashtra. The juxtaposition of the ancient Buddhist caves with the bustling, vibrant Hindu temple provides a unique cultural insight. Visitors must climb about 500 steps to reach the temple, which offers breathtaking views of the surrounding valley alongside its spiritual aura.</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-700 mb-5">
    <li><strong>Things to do:</strong> Seek blessings, experience the local culture, and enjoy the valley views from the hilltop.</li>
    <li><strong>Best time to visit:</strong> Early mornings to avoid the heat during the steep climb. Avoid Navratri if you dislike heavy crowds.</li>
    <li><strong>How to reach:</strong> Located right next to the Karla Caves; a short drive from Lonavala.</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-800 mt-8 mb-3 leading-snug font-display"><strong>19. Korigad Fort</strong></h3>
<figure class="my-4"><img src="images/ChatGPT-Image-Jul-4-2025-09_47_19-PM-1024x683.webp" alt="Korigad Fort" class="w-full rounded-lg shadow-md"></figure>
<p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed mb-5">Located near the luxury township of Aamby Valley, Korigad Fort is a hill fort that remains relatively intact compared to others in the region. The massive plateau on top houses a couple of serene lakes and the Korai Devi temple. The trek to Korigad is straightforward, involving well-laid stone steps, making it perfect for novice trekkers. Once atop, the fort provides a stunning 360-degree view of the verdant surroundings and the Aamby Valley city below.</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-700 mb-5">
    <li><strong>Things to do:</strong> Easy trekking, exploring the two crater lakes on the fort, and viewing the massive cannons.</li>
    <li><strong>Best time to visit:</strong> Monsoon for an ethereal experience amidst the clouds.</li>
    <li><strong>How to reach:</strong> The base village of Peth Shahpur is about 20 kilometers from Lonavala on the Aamby Valley road.</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-800 mt-8 mb-3 leading-snug font-display"><strong>20. Imagicaa Water Park & Theme Park</strong></h3>
<figure class="my-4"><img src="images/aquamagica.webp" alt="Imagicaa Lonavala" class="w-full rounded-lg shadow-md"></figure>
<p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed mb-5">While technically situated in Khopoli (on the expressway on the way to Lonavala), Imagicaa is a world-class entertainment destination that deserves a spot on your itinerary. It boasts a sprawling theme park with international standard roller coasters, a massive water park with thrilling slides, and a snow park. It is a fantastic, full-day detour for families looking for high-octane entertainment and joyrides.</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-700 mb-5">
    <li><strong>Things to do:</strong> Ride the Nitro roller coaster, float in the lazy river, and enjoy the grand evening parade.</li>
    <li><strong>Best time to visit:</strong> Year-round. Summers are perfect for the water park, while winters are great for the theme park.</li>
    <li><strong>How to reach:</strong> Located right off the Mumbai-Pune Expressway at the Khalapur Toll Plaza.</li>
</ul>


